@71011 = ~Dead Magic~
@71012 = ~Dead Magic (Abjuration)
Level: 10
Range: 0
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 12-meter radius
Saving Throw: none

The spell Dead Magic is the ultimate disjunction spell. When it is cast by the warlord, a wave of entropic force sweeps and covers an area extending 12 meters around him. The power of Dead Magic has several different effects:
- All magic effects are dispelled on the caster, regardless of the level and there is no saving throw allowed.
- All magic effects are dispelled within the area, with a spell level of 40, and still with a 1% chance of failure.
- All summoned creatures are irrevocably sent back.
- All arcane spellcasters within the area (except the caster) forget 1D6 spells.
- All charged magical items within the area (except those of the caster) lose 1d4 charges.
Moreover, the wave persists for some time, creating for 3 rounds an anti-magic area where every spell that is cast automatically fails. This area also affects the warlord.~
